\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Confirmatory observed $\rho $ (diamonds) against 300 shared donor-permutation nulls per arm (violins; bars mark null q95). Two null designs are shown: for the non-B2 arms the donor ridge is fit on permuted targets over frozen features and centers near zero; for B2 the encoder is \emph  {retrained} on permuted endpoint labels and evaluated honestly --- its shifted distribution (red, mean $\approx 0.3$) measures signal reachable through non-endpoint channels, not a failed null. A separate readout-permuted check on B2's frozen features centers at zero (text).}}{9}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:null}{{3}{9}{Confirmatory observed $\rho $ (diamonds) against 300 shared donor-permutation nulls per arm (violins; bars mark null q95). Two null designs are shown: for the non-B2 arms the donor ridge is fit on permuted targets over frozen features and centers near zero; for B2 the encoder is \emph {retrained} on permuted endpoint labels and evaluated honestly --- its shifted distribution (red, mean $\approx 0.3$) measures signal reachable through non-endpoint channels, not a failed null. A separate readout-permuted check on B2's frozen features centers at zero (text)}{figure.caption.10}{}}
